#
# Use ThinLTO instead of full LTO.
# Merged by: kernel/build-kernel.sh -L (used by the GitHub Actions build)
#
# GKI's default full LTO links vmlinux in a single process that needs about
# 16 GB of RAM, which is all a free GitHub-hosted runner has. ThinLTO links
# in parallel with a fraction of the memory. LTO mode does not change the
# kernel module ABI (KMI symbols and CRCs), and CFI stays enabled.
#
CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_THIN=y
# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG_FULL is not set
